    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="overview" class="doc-h2">1. Overview</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Any logged-in user can add Health Kitchen to their account the same way they add
                ENCY or beekeeping. The feature uses the inventory system as a pantry of foods and herbs,
                ENCY rows as the scientific/culinary detail for each item, and the v2 AI stack to build
                menus and daily activity plans from the symptoms that are <strong>active right now</strong>.
                Recipes are constrained to what is actually in the pantry and to current ENCY data,
                optionally augmented by AI learning and net search (trust-tiered, never auto-authoritative).
            </p>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Branch of record: <code class="doc-code">ency</code> (worktree port 4011).
                Schema materialization belongs on the <code class="doc-code">schema</code> branch.
                Inventory category work belongs on InventoryAccounting.
                AI prompt/recall/search extensions belong on <code class="doc-code">aisystem</code>
                if they cannot be done as thin additions here — raise, do not absorb.
            </p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="existing" class="doc-h2">2. What already exists (summarized, then mapped)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">This section states the live code first, then the mapping. Mapping-only would pretend these files were not read.</p>

            <h3 class="doc-h3">2.1 Membership / add-ons</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">
                <code class="doc-code">Comserv::Controller::Admin::SiteModules</code>
                <code class="doc-code">_default_addon_catalog</code> already lists
                <code class="doc-code">ency</code> (Encyclopedia &amp; Herbal Database, route <code class="doc-code">/ency</code>)
                and <code class="doc-code">beekeeping</code> (BMaster, route <code class="doc-code">/apiary</code>).
                Access is <code class="doc-code">MembershipHelper::can_access($module)</code>:
                (1) <code class="doc-code">membership_service_access</code> per-user override,
                (2) plan_benefits, (3) legacy plan flags such as <code class="doc-code">has_beekeeping</code>.
                Site enablement is <code class="doc-code">SiteModule</code> plus hosting
                <code class="doc-code">requested_addons</code> in <code class="doc-code">Pages.pm</code>.
                Nav catalog already gates Beekeeping with <code class="doc-code">requires_module =&gt; 'beekeeping'</code>.
            </p>
            <p class="doc-body"><strong>Mapping:</strong> add catalog key <code class="doc-code">healthkitchen</code> (D2), reuse the same three-layer access check, add a member-facing enable action so it is not admin-only, gate new nav the same way.</p>

            <h3 class="doc-h3">2.2 ENCY knowledge graph</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Live tables (Result classes under <code class="doc-code">Model/Schema/Ency/Result/Ency/</code>):
            </p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Result / table</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">What it already holds</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code class="doc-code">Herb</code> / <code class="doc-code">ency_herb_tb</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Botanical identity, culinary, therapeutic_action, medical_uses, dosage, contra_indications, formulas, constituents, pollinator fields</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td"><code class="doc-code">Symptom</code> / <code class="doc-code">ency_symptom_tb</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Named symptoms, body_system, severity, host_type</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code class="doc-code">HerbSymptom</code> / <code class="doc-code">herb_symptom</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Herb ↔ symptom with relationship_type + notes</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td"><code class="doc-code">Formula</code> / <code class="doc-code">usbm_formula_tb</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Named formulas/recipes; nav alias <code class="doc-code">/ENCY/recipes</code> already redirects here. Linked via FormulaHerb</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Drug / Disease junctions</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Drug–herb interactions, herb–disease; planner must consult these before suggesting an item</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body"><strong>Mapping (D3):</strong> do not invent a parallel food CMS. Link each pantry SKU to Herb, Organism, Animal, Insect, and/or Formula so birds/animals/insects can be foods too. User “active symptoms” reference <code class="doc-code">ency_symptom_tb.record_id</code>.</p>

            <h3 class="doc-h3">2.3 Inventory</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">
                <code class="doc-code">inventory_items</code> is sitename-scoped with
                <code class="doc-code">category</code>, <code class="doc-code">item_origin</code>,
                <code class="doc-code">unit_of_measure</code>, <code class="doc-code">is_consumable</code>,
                stock fields. There is no food/herb category and no FK to ENCY on this branch.
            </p>
            <p class="doc-body"><strong>Mapping:</strong> pantry reads available qty from inventory (or a user overlay — D1). Junction table <code class="doc-code">inventory_ency_map</code> owned here; category list change is raised on InventoryAccounting.</p>

            <h3 class="doc-h3">2.4 AI</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">
                v2 prompts live in <code class="doc-code">Comserv::Model::AI2::Prompts</code>
                (bmaster already ported). <code class="doc-code">agents.json</code> is picker/permissions only.
                <code class="doc-code">AI2::KnowledgeRecall</code> injects trust-tiered prior knowledge
                (<code class="doc-code">VERIFIED</code> / <code class="doc-code">UNVERIFIED</code> / <code class="doc-code">INTERNAL</code>).
                <code class="doc-code">AI2::Search</code> is SearXNG, <strong>disabled by default</strong>
                in <code class="doc-code">root/config/services.json</code>.
                ENCY controller already has herb/symptom AI editor workflows.
            </p>
            <p class="doc-body"><strong>Mapping:</strong> add <code class="doc-code">build_healthkitchen</code>. Planner first runs a deterministic Util (pantry ∩ herb_symptom). LLM only composes the menu/activity text and may propose ENCY edits as unverified staging. Search never overwrites contra_indications.</p>

            <h3 class="doc-h3">2.5 Projects already in the DB</h3>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Id</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Code</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Role in this plan</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">108</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">ENCY</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Parent encyclopedia project</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">109</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">formulas</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Existing recipe/formula system — Health Kitchen consumes it, does not fork it</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">227</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">HealthManagementSystem.</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Empty Requested child of 108; this plan attaches here (D5). Zero todos today</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">199</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">HEALTH-PLAN</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Server health — out of scope</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-50">
            <h2 id="prerequisites" class="doc-h2">3. Prerequisites</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li>Logged-in user; membership or service-access grant</li>
                <li>Site may enable <code class="doc-code">ency</code> (knowledge) independently of Health Kitchen</li>
                <li>Inventory items exist (or user overlay, D1)</li>
                <li>Schema-compare available on schema branch for new tables</li>
                <li>AI2 chat on the ency worktree server (port 4011)</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="col-50">
            <h2 id="features" class="doc-h2">4. Key Features</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Opt-in add-on</strong> — same catalog as ENCY / beekeeping</li>
                <li><strong>Pantry</strong> — foods/herbs with qty, linked to ENCY detail</li>
                <li><strong>Active symptoms</strong> — user-owned, FK to ENCY symptoms</li>
                <li><strong>Menus + activity plans</strong> — constrained to pantry ∩ knowledge</li>
                <li><strong>AI compose</strong> — v2 agent; knowledge + optional search, trust-tiered</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="architecture" class="doc-h2">5. Architecture</h2>
            <div class="doc-codebox"><pre>User enable (membership_service_access / plan_benefits)
        -&gt; HealthKitchen controller (thin)
            -&gt; Util::HealthKitchen (deterministic match)
            -&gt; inventory_items (+ overlay if D1)
            -&gt; inventory_ency_map -&gt; ency_herb_tb / usbm_formula_tb
            -&gt; user_active_symptom -&gt; ency_symptom_tb / herb_symptom
            -&gt; AI2::Prompts::build_healthkitchen
                 + KnowledgeRecall + Search (optional, UNVERIFIED)
            -&gt; persist UserHealthPlan / meal slots / activities
ENCY editors still own herb/formula truth; AI only stages suggestions.</pre></div>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">What we gain</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">What we give up</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">One pantry + one encyclopedia instead of a third food CMS</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">No automatic clinical advice; no silent wiki overwrites from the web</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Same enablement UX as beekeeping/ENCY</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">New tables wait on schema-compare; ency cannot CREATE TABLE in prod</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-warning">Biggest loss if we skip the Util and go LLM-only: recipes that mention foods the user does not have, and suggestions that ignore contra_indications. The deterministic intersect is the load-bearing gate; the model only writes prose around it.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="workstreams" class="doc-h2">6. Workstreams (named sub-projects, not “Phase N”)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Each workstream becomes a <strong>sub-project</strong> of HEALTHKITCHEN (or of #227 if D5 keeps this doc on 227). Steps become todos. Gate is observable.</p>

            <h3 id="ws-enable" class="doc-h3">HK-ENABLE — add-on + nav</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">Catalog key, MembershipHelper, member self-serve grant, TopDropListENCY (or Member) links. <strong>GATE:</strong> user without grant cannot see <code class="doc-code">/healthkitchen</code>; user with grant can.</p>

            <h3 id="ws-pantry" class="doc-h3">HK-PANTRY — inventory link</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">Junction Result + pantry UI + InventoryAccounting category ticket. <strong>GATE:</strong> a stocked SKU shows its ENCY herb page and is visible to the planner as available.</p>
            <p class="doc-body"><strong>Stock in:</strong> sitename inventory is filled by the existing AP receive path (<code class="doc-code">/Inventory/invoice</code>). Coop purchase-invoice <em>emails</em> are already classified on the InventoryAccounting worktree (<code class="doc-code">MailInvoiceClassifier</code> → <code class="doc-code">/mail/classify_invoices</code> → JSON). That classifier does <em>not</em> yet parse line items into <code class="doc-code">inventory_items</code>. Health Kitchen must not fork a second receive pipeline: when email→AP lines exist, pantry qty follows stock receive. Until then, seed SKUs + UserPantryQty overlay for personal use.</p>

            <h3 id="first-drink" class="doc-h3">First daily drink (user 2026-09-23) — seed recipe, not coded yet</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">Morning pot: 4 demitasse; half the usual coffee dose; drink 2 cups. This is a <code class="doc-code">usbm_formula_tb</code> recipe whose components are inventory SKUs (some ENCY herbs). Votes Coffee is a supplier, not the coop.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Ingredient</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Source / notes</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">ENCY / pantry</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Coffee beans</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Votes Coffee, Vernon — CAD 65 / 5 lb bag</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Purchased SKU + supplier; organism (coffee plant) optional</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Turmeric</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Coop invoice line when present</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Herb (culinary + therapeutic)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Ceylon cinnamon</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Coop invoice line when present</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Herb — distinct from cassia</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Black pepper</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Pinch ground now; later whole pepper + mill</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Herb; two SKUs (ground vs whole) when mill lands</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Chia seed</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Small amount; coop when present</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Organism / seed food, not herb-only</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Organika enhanced collagen protein</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Scoop; coop or other vendor</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Purchased SKU (food, not a medication)</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-muted">Planner treats this as a breakfast/tea slot formula. Do not auto-write ENCY contra_indications from web search. Collagen is food, not a drug; never suggest stopping prescriptions.</p>

            <h3 id="ws-symptoms" class="doc-h3">HK-SYMPTOMS — active set</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">Profile + active-symptom rows FK to ENCY. <strong>GATE:</strong> resolving a symptom removes it from the next plan generation input.</p>

            <h3 id="ws-planner" class="doc-h3">HK-PLANNER — menus and daily activity</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">Deterministic Util first; then <code class="doc-code">build_healthkitchen</code>; persist plan; dashboard. Daily activity = sleep/movement/hydration/forage-prep style tasks stored on <code class="doc-code">user_health_activity</code> — not CSC planning todos. <strong>GATE:</strong> generated menu contains only pantry-available, non-contraindicated items for the active symptom set.</p>

            <h3 id="ws-knowledge" class="doc-h3">HK-KNOWLEDGE — augment, do not overwrite</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">Search/learning writes staging notes with source URL + UNVERIFIED. Editor applies to herb/formula. <strong>GATE:</strong> running refresh does not change <code class="doc-code">contra_indications</code> until an editor saves.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="schema" class="doc-h2">7. Proposed Result classes (schema branch creates tables)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Source of truth = Result files on ency; DDL only via in-app schema-compare on schema. Never hand SQL.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Class / table</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Purpose</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code class="doc-code">InventoryEncyMap</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">inventory_item_id; nullable herb_id, organism_id, animal_id, insect_id, formula_id; sitename</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td"><code class="doc-code">UserHealthProfile</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">user_id, sitename, diet flags, allergies (text), goals</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code class="doc-code">UserActiveSymptom</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">user_id, symptom_id, severity, status active/resolved, started_at</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td"><code class="doc-code">UserHealthPlan</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">generated plan header, source (util/ai), trust summary, JSON body</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code class="doc-code">UserMealSlot</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">plan_id, date, slot (breakfast/lunch/dinner/tea), formula_id or free text, inventory ids used</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td"><code class="doc-code">UserHealthActivity</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">plan_id, date, activity text, done flag</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code class="doc-code">UserPantryQty</code> (D1 — required)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">user_id, inventory_item_id, qty, unit — personal overlay; sitename inventory is separate household stock</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="safety" class="doc-h2">8. Safety (non-negotiable)</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li>This is a <strong>wellness and kitchen planner</strong>, not diagnosis or treatment.</li>
                <li>Every generated plan page shows a disclaimer and a link to ENCY contra_indications / drug–herb rows used.</li>
                <li>Never suggest stopping a prescribed drug. If a drug–herb row exists, exclude or warn.</li>
                <li>Do not promote medications that interfere with health (D4).</li>
                <li>Web/AI text is labelled UNVERIFIED until an editor prefixes VERIFIED.</li>
                <li>Public users never see INTERNAL knowledge (KnowledgeRecall rule).</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="project-tracking" class="doc-h2">9. Project Tracking</h2>
            <div class="doc-success">
                <p class="doc-body">
                    Owning project:
